.TH MAN 1 "2026-08-16" "notcoreutils" "notcoreutils Manual"
.SH NAME
man \- a minimal manual-page viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B man
[\fISECTION\fR] \fINAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B man
finds NAME's page under the usual manN/ tree (honoring
.IR $MANPATH ,
falling back to the standard FHS locations), gunzips it if needed
(this project's own deflate.h, manually skipping the gzip wrapper),
and renders the common troff/man(7) macros as plain readable text.
.PP
Deliberately not a groff reimplementation \- no macro expansion
language, no tables (.TS/.TE), no real fill/adjust (line wrapping),
no font metrics. Handles what the overwhelming majority of real man
pages actually use:
.BR .TH / .SH / .SS
headers,
.BR .PP / .P / .LP / .TP
paragraph breaks,
.BR .B / .I / .BR / .IR / .RB / .RI
alternating bold/italic (rendered as ANSI bold/underline), the
backslash\-f family of inline font escapes,
.BR .nf / .fi
literal blocks,
.BR .RS / .RE
indent, and the common backslash\-dash and named\-character escapes
used in running text. Unknown macros are skipped rather than printed
raw \- honest omission beats dumping troff source.
.PP
Pages written for this project's own tools use the classic man(7)
macro set documented above, not mdoc (.Dd/.Dt/.Nm/.Op/.Fl/.Ar/.Bl/
.It/.El) \- mdoc is a separate macro package this renderer does not
speak, so an mdoc\-formatted page (as sbase/ubase's own upstream
pages use) will render incompletely here.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MANPATH
Colon\-separated list of manN/ tree roots to search, tried before
the standard FHS locations.
